00:00:19.609 --> 00:00:25.300
where at the time Wei Yi was playing in the
Challenger's section. He went on to win that

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:30.380
which earned him the right to play in this
year's Master's section. So this game here

00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:37.800
acts as the first meeting between these two.
Wei Yi, a 16-year-old from China, clearly

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:43.030
one of the most talented rising stars in our
game. He is paired against our current World

00:00:43.030 --> 00:00:50.430
Chess Champion, the 25-year-old Magnus Carlsen
from Norway. Let's see what would happen in

00:00:50.430 --> 00:01:00.920
this first of 'many' encounters? e4 e5 knight
f3, knight c6, bishop b5 entering the Ruy

00:01:00.930 --> 00:01:10.600
