the position does become sharp. It does...does

00:01:34.750 --> 00:01:43.510
have tension in it...it does open up as early
as move 8. Knight f6, castles, bishop e7, rook

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:52.390
e1, b5, bishop b3, black castles, and after
c3...d5. So okay...here we are. This is a

00:01:52.390 --> 00:02:00.130
sharp line in this opening, namely the Marshall
Attack. This is a gambit line. Black is with

00:02:00.130 --> 00:02:05.760
this move offering up a pawn. Black with this
move is opening up the position, creating

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:17.150
pawn tension. And with this line black tries
to show that this backward, or delay in the

00:02:17.150 --> 00:02:25.700
white development is an issue. e takes d,
knight takes, knight takes e. White's now

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:35.840
up a pawn. Knight takes knight, rook takes,
black secures the knight's post, d3. We're

00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:45.319
